id: questions/open-questions
title: "What is still unresolved?"
kind: lacuna-index
status: preview
updated: 2026-09-12

purpose: >
  Keep unanswered, disputed, deferred, and decision-changing questions visible
  so the repository or observing agent does not manufacture closure.

template: templates/open-question.yawn

open_questions:
  - question: "When is yawn-ai/web-game archived, and which inbound links and integrations must move to yawn-ai/yawn.bot first?"
    coordinate: "runtime/repository-identity"
    why_it_matters: "Dave stated on 2026-09-12 that web-game is the older repository and is to be archived. Archiving is reversible on GitHub, but it breaks nothing only if every live pointer already names yawn.bot; the pointers in this repository were corrected the same day, the ones outside it are uninventoried."
    evidence_needed:
      - inbound link inventory
      - Vercel and GitHub integration inventory
      - archive receipt
    owner: Dave
    status: open
    blocks_action: false
    review_after: "before archiving the repository"

  - question: "Which exact .yawn protocol revision should govern the official YAWN.bot runtime?"
    coordinate: "runtime/protocol-pin"
    why_it_matters: "The runtime must not silently change behavior when the public protocol evolves."
    evidence_needed:
      - accepted public protocol commit
      - compatibility result against the runtime
    owner: Dave
    status: open
    blocks_action: true
    review_after: "before canonical production reconciliation"

  - question: "Which YAWN.bot contracts are public protocol and which remain private implementation?"
    coordinate: "public-private-boundary"
    why_it_matters: "The public repo should teach portable coherence without exposing private memory or proprietary implementation."
    evidence_needed:
      - secret and private-reference scan
      - public contract inventory
      - owner-reviewed promotion list
    owner: Dave
    status: open
    blocks_action: true
    review_after: "before public publication"

  - question: "What is the first production projection-equivalence receipt?"
    coordinate: "runtime/projection-proof"
    why_it_matters: "Wallet, phone, desktop, and world surfaces must share one orientation revision and authority state."
    evidence_needed:
      - authenticated runtime fixture
      - wallet and desktop screenshots
      - orientation revision comparison
      - console and runtime logs
    owner: YAWN.bot
    status: open
    blocks_action: true
    review_after: "before declaring production healthy"

recently_resolved:
  - question: "Should the official YAWN.bot GitHub repository slug change from web-game to yawn-bot?"
    answer: "Yes. The official YAWN.bot runtime is https://github.com/yawn-ai/yawn.bot with its Supabase database; https://github.com/yawn-ai/web-game is the older address, superseded and to be archived. Stated by Dave on 2026-09-12 and recorded on his behalf; provisional until he confirms it in a record he writes."
    status: answered-provisionally
    epistemic_status: reported
    owner: Dave
    answered_on: 2026-09-12
    proof_refs:
      - migrations/2026-09-12-cohere-vocabulary-and-attribution.yawn
      - yawn.yawn
      - agents/yawn.bot.yawn
    supersedes:
      - "Which codebase is the official YAWN.bot runtime? (2026-07-11 answer naming web-game)"
  - question: "Which codebase is the official YAWN.bot runtime?"
    answer: "The codebase at https://github.com/yawn-ai/web-game is the official YAWN.bot runtime."
    status: superseded
    superseded_on: 2026-09-12
    superseded_by: "the repository-slug answer above; the same codebase is now addressed at https://github.com/yawn-ai/yawn.bot"
    owner: Dave
    proof_refs:
      - records/yawn-bot-runtime-promotion-2026-07-11.yawn

states:
  - open
  - answered-with-evidence
  - answered-provisionally
  - disputed
  - deferred
  - superseded

rules:
  - "An unanswered question remains visible."
  - "A provisional answer is labeled provisional."
  - "Corrections supersede interpretations without erasing source history."
  - "Questions that do not change a decision need not block movement."

connects:
  lacuna: core/lacuna.yawn
  question_packets: question-packets/node.yawn
  feedback: feedback/form.yawn
  next_moves: records/next-move-ledger.yawn
  runtime_promotion: records/yawn-bot-runtime-promotion-2026-07-11.yawn
